# Per-entry justified ignores for the GATING Trivy scan only (see
# .github/workflows/ci.yml -- the non-gating "full report" scan does
# NOT read this file, so every entry here stays visible there and in
# SECURITY_VULNERABILITY_STATUS.md instead of silently disappearing).
# No blanket ignores. Each entry must have a CVE, a reason, and a
# review date; remove the entry the day a real fix lands.

# CVE-2026-0994 -- protobuf (google.protobuf.json_format.ParseDict
# recursion-depth bypass, DoS via deeply nested Any messages).
# Installed: protobuf==4.25.9 (transitive, pinned by mediapipe==0.10.14
# which requires protobuf<5). Fixed in 5.29.6 / 6.33.5, but mediapipe
# only supports those from 0.10.30+, which removed the legacy
# mediapipe.solutions API this app's FaceLandmarkExtractor (app/cv/
# face_landmarks.py) depends on -- upgrading requires migrating to
# mediapipe's Tasks API and vendoring a separately-distributed .task
# model asset, a real rewrite of the core facial-analysis pipeline.
# Not reachable here regardless: this app never calls
# google.protobuf.json_format.ParseDict on attacker-supplied input --
# mediapipe uses protobuf only for its own internal binary configs.
# See SECURITY_VULNERABILITY_STATUS.md and CI_SECURITY_RECONCILIATION.md
# for the full writeup. Review by: 2026-12-09 (re-check whether a
# mediapipe release has since restored solutions-API compatibility
# with a patched protobuf, or reassess the Tasks API migration).
CVE-2026-0994
